{"w":2400,"h":3406,"lines":[{"w":0.062144451141357443,"c":1,"t":"Test 2","x":0.069958702158243902,"y":0.052014827513303663,"h":0.015156390872760439},{"x":0.068041242782083108,"t":"And what about artists such as Mondrian, whose paintings consist exclusively of horizontal","w":0.85979380289713536,"y":0.097383720654576456,"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"and vertical lines encasing blocks of colour? Mondrian's works are deceptively simple, but","x":0.068041232815718902,"w":0.84742268880208327,"h":0.017455516530707205,"y":0.11626541397308998},{"y":0.13505578403881691,"w":0.88247426350911462,"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"x":0.068041218662271863,"t":"eye-tracking studies confirm that they are meticulously composed, and that simply rotating a"},{"w":0.87835052490234367,"x":0.068041232283370709,"y":0.15406976760909608,"h":0.015988371754420694,"t":"piece radically changes the way we view it. With the originals, volunteers eyes tended to stay","c":1},{"w":0.85773193359375,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"y":0.17146212560456009,"t":"longer on certain places in the image, but with the altered versions they would flit across a","x":0.065979393899117819},{"x":0.068041255887161756,"y":0.19040697691157482,"w":0.88659790039062503,"t":"piece more rapidly. As a result, the volunteers considered the altered versions less pleasurable","h":0.015993492923900177,"c":1},{"y":0.20930232574468599,"c":1,"x":0.068041233605864351,"t":"when they later rated the work.","w":0.30103093465169273,"h":0.015988371754420694},{"c":1,"t":"In a similar study, Oshin Vartanian of Toronto University asked volunteers to compare original","x":0.065979363012657471,"y":0.24563953505069158,"h":0.015988371754420583,"w":0.88247426350911451},{"y":0.26453317657538544,"t":"paintings with ones which he had altered by moving objects around within the frame. He","x":0.068041239632885317,"w":0.8453608194986979,"h":0.017443567881917366,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"found that almost everyone preferred the original, whether it was a Van Gogh still life or","w":0.83092783610026033,"y":0.28332354664117387,"h":0.01614797416324143,"x":0.068041236481388226},{"h":0.017441859892096456,"x":0.06804125358791055,"w":0.84329895019531242,"y":0.30087209309174245,"c":1,"t":"an abstract by Miró. Vartanian also found that changing the composition of the paintings"},{"t":"reduced activation in those brain areas linked with meaning and interpretation.","h":0.019180163452363397,"c":1,"y":0.31872020521686184,"x":0.065901705179171211,"w":0.75687906901041657},{"w":0.82075729370117179,"h":0.019857630614875998,"t":"In another experiment, Alex Forsythe of the University of Liverpool analysed the visual","c":1,"x":0.063849566068001212,"y":0.35439288586485029},{"t":"intricacy of different pieces of art, and her results suggest that many artists use a key level of","x":0.065979390267127749,"w":0.87422678629557282,"y":0.37492659984163978,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.015988371754420694,"y":0.39389534900459355,"w":0.86185567220052073,"x":0.0680412359618425,"t":"detail to please the brain. Too little and the work is boring, but too much results in a kind of"},{"w":0.89278350830078113,"h":0.017446128186658805,"y":0.41133294185168967,"t":"'perceptual overload, according to Forsythe. What's more, appealing pieces both abstract and","c":1,"x":0.065979379793060858},{"t":"representational, show signs of'fractals' - repeated motifs recurring in different scales. Fractals","h":0.019083969465648831,"y":0.42865531459251083,"x":0.065979377937238348,"w":0.89278350830078135,"c":1},{"t":"are common throughout nature, for example in the shapes of mountain peaks or the branches","h":0.017441861012089777,"x":0.065979372986219198,"y":0.44912790669894009,"w":0.89484537760416671,"c":1},{"t":"of trees. It is possible that our visual system, which evolved in the great outdoors, finds it","w":0.8391752624511718,"h":0.017467465179497155,"c":1,"x":0.065979378975071848,"y":0.46799765137072136},{"y":0.4867880212788156,"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"x":0.06597939161661534,"t":"easier to process such patterns.","w":0.30103090922037756},{"x":0.065979359870809537,"w":0.86804128011067716,"t":"It is also intriguing that the brain appears to process movement when we see a handwritten","y":0.52319436288611243,"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.017449541926313983,"x":0.063917528289045913,"w":0.84536081949869801,"t":"letter, as if we are replaying the writer's moment of creation. This has led some to wonder","y":0.54215116251502526},{"c":1,"h":0.015988371754420583,"x":0.065979356172667855,"t":"whether Pollock's works feel so dynamic because the brain reconstructs the energetic actions","y":0.56104651179514253,"w":0.88453613281249999},{"c":1,"t":"the artist used as he painted. This may be down to our brain's'mirror neurons, which are","w":0.83298970540364581,"y":0.57839107462776873,"h":0.017615971814445075,"x":0.063917518649379876},{"h":0.019542396173572452,"y":0.5953520858997382,"c":1,"x":0.06591546738221761,"w":0.88466654459635408,"t":"known to mimic others' actions. The hypothesis will need to be thoroughly tested, however. It"},{"c":1,"x":0.065939257242989505,"y":0.61490006255982455,"t":"might even be the case that we could use neuroaesthetic studies to understand the longevity","w":0.88462605794270832,"h":0.018845666245859816},{"c":1,"w":0.82483886718749988,"x":0.065936711719095625,"y":0.63367911598313675,"t":"of some pieces of artwork. While the fashions of the time might shape what is currently","h":0.018853434519563339},{"w":0.84754435221354152,"h":0.020287094295409869,"c":1,"x":0.065913770181666387,"y":0.65152841488335522,"t":"popular, works that are best adapted to our visual system may be the most likely to linger"},{"x":0.063815586358475299,"w":0.58785975138346358,"h":0.021159762854584541,"t":"once the trends of previous generations have been forgotten.","y":0.66946681961432097,"c":1},{"x":0.063853815180490769,"w":0.88671854654947913,"c":1,"y":0.7061857841583028,"t":"It's still early days for the field of neuroaesthetics - and these studies are probably only a taste","h":0.01938280832466488},{"w":0.89690724690755208,"c":1,"t":"of what is to come. It would, however, be foolish to reduce art appreciation to a set of scientific","x":0.063917510463994062,"h":0.017615971814445075,"y":0.72665883723960822},{"w":0.88247426350911473,"t":"laws. We shouldn't underestimate the importance of the style of a particular artist, their place","h":0.015988371754420583,"x":0.063917507298049916,"c":1,"y":0.74563953505045177},{"h":0.015990078624248172,"c":1,"w":0.87216491699218757,"x":0.063917541400813419,"y":0.76453317701851409,"t":"in history and the artistic environment of their time. Abstract art offers both a challenge and"},{"x":0.065979412383081054,"t":"the freedom to play with different interpretations. In some ways, it's not so different to science,","c":1,"h":0.017615971814445186,"y":0.78185554921681677,"w":0.89690714518229164},{"t":"where we are constantly looking for systems and decoding meaning so that we can view and","y":0.80087209274684246,"h":0.017441861012089777,"x":0.065979369848287395,"c":1,"w":0.88041239420572914},{"t":"appreciate the world in a new way.","h":0.018493991141730892,"y":0.81881540843512779,"c":1,"x":0.063804315430807612,"w":0.33426958719889321},{"c":1,"y":0.95639534893989231,"x":0.063917525604558462,"w":0.028865979512532558,"h":0.015988371754420694,"t":"50"},{"x":0.35209807542691846,"h":0.023629227177367373,"t":"leltsresources.org","c":1,"w":0.29172538757324212,"y":0.9533535444102853}]}